<<16>> Give me an algebra exercise for a 6th grade student learning mathematics. It should be an exercise on evaluating expressions. It should have multiple steps. There should be marks/points assigned to the question. It should be a with Answer. <<Prompt>>
<<16>> Evaluate each of the following expressions when \( x = 10 \) and \( y = 5 \). (2 marks each)

\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item \( x + y = \_\_\_ \)
\item \( x - y = \_\_\_ \)
\item \( x \times y = \_\_\_ \)
\item \( x + 2y = \_\_\_ \)
\item \( 3x + 2y = \_\_\_ \)
\item \( 3x - 2y = \_\_\_ \)
\end{enumerate}

\subsection*{Answers}
\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item \( x + y = 15 \)
\item \( x - y = 5 \)
\item \( x \times y = 50 \)
\item \( x + 2y = 20 \)
\item \( 3x + 2y = 40 \)
\item \( 3x - 2y = 30 \)
\end{enumerate} <<Generation>>
<<17>> Give me an algebra exercise for a 6th grade student learning mathematics. It should be an exercise on algebraic expressions. It should have multiple steps. <<Prompt>>
<<17>> Given the following algebraic expressions:

\begin{enumerate}[label=\Roman*.]
\item \( 4b + 2 \)
\item \( 6c + 3 \)
\item \( 5d + 4 \)
\item \( 3e + 2 \)
\end{enumerate}

\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item What is the value of the first expression if \( b = 3 \)?
\item What is the value of the second expression if \( c = 2 \)?
\item What is the value of the third expression if \( d = 4 \)?
\item What is the value of the fourth expression if \( e = 5 \)?
\end{enumerate} <<Generation>>
