\item I new the answer.
\item I write with my right hand.
\item I right the wrongs.
\item I hear the music.
\item I here the music.
\item I have four books.
\item I have fore books.
\end{enumerate} Now rewrite the sentences you crossed in 3, so that they make sense. Use the correct homophone in each case.\\
