ample from my life is a plug. The plastic in the plug stops the electricity from reaching me." Tell the class what you have learned about electricity and safety. Use examples from your life. For example, "I have learned that electricity can be dangerous. An example from my life is a plug. The plastic in the plug stops the electricity from reaching me and keeps me safe." Think of a reason why we do not use metal plugs. Write a sentence to describe this reason. For example, "We do not use metal plugs because they conduct electricity and can kill us." Think of a reason why we do not use rubber wires. Write a sentence to describe this reason. For example, "We do not use rubber wires because they do not conduct electricity." Explain why it is important for wires to conduct electricity. Write a sentence to describe why it is important. For example, "It is important for wires to conduct electricity so that electricity reaches the lights and they light up." Tell the class what you have learned about electricity and conductors. Use examples from your life. For example, "I have learned that electricity needs to reach lights so that they light up. An example from my life is a lamp. The metal wire in the lamp conducts electricity so that the lamp lights up." Explain how the electricity reaches the lamp. Write a sentence to describe how electricity reaches the lamp. For example, "Electricity reaches the lamp through the wire." Explain how the electricity reaches the bulb. Write a sentence to describe how electricity reaches the bulb. For example, "Electricity reaches the bulb through the wire." Explain what happens when electricity reaches the bulb. Write a sentence to describe what happens. For example, "When electricity reaches the bulb it lights up." Tell the class what you have learned about electricity and bulbs. Use examples from your life. For example, "I have learned that electricity lights up bulbs. An example from my life is a lamp. Electricity reaches the bulb in the 