<<69>> You are talking with a friend about your daily routine.\\
You are both asking each other what time you do certain things.\\
Kijk: What time do you get up? I get up at half past six.\\
What time do you get up?\\
You could ask each other: What time do you have breakfast/dinner/supper?\\
What time do you go to the cinema/ go to bed/ do the shopping?\\
Answer each other's questions using the information in brackets.\\
For example:\\
What time do you go to the cinema? (I go at eight o'clock.)\\
I go to the cinema at eight o'clock.

\begin{enumerate}
\item What time do you have breakfast? (I have breakfast at 8:00.)
\item What time do you go shopping? (I go shopping at 2:00.)
\item What time do you have dinner? (I have dinner at 6:00.)
\item What time do you go to bed? (I go to bed at 11:00.)
\item What time do you do the washing up? (I do the washing up at 7:00.)
\item What time do you watch television? (I watch television at 9:00.)
\item What time do you work out? (I work out at 10:00.)
\item What time do you read the paper? (I read the paper at 12:00.)
\end{enumerate}

\subsection*{Answers}
\begin{enumerate}
\item Ik heb om acht uur ontbijt.
\item Ik ga om twee uur winkelen.
\item Ik eet om zes uur avondeten.
\item Ik ga om elf uur naar bed.
\item Ik doe om zeven uur de afwas.
\item Ik kijk om negen uur televisie.
\item Ik werk om tien uur.
\item Ik lees om twaalf uur de krant.
\end{enumerate} <<Generation>>
