<<701>> Give me a short answer exercise for a 2nd grade student learning computer science. <<Prompt>>
<<701>> Open a spreadsheet.  
\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item Click on the tab called 'Sheet1' to open it.  
\item Change the name of 'Sheet1' to 'My sheet'.  
\end{enumerate}  
Save your work.  

How can you make a copy of a sheet in a spreadsheet? Describe the steps you would take to create a copy. Think about what actions you need to do on the computer to achieve this. Write down your description of the process.  

Describe how you would change the name of a sheet in a spreadsheet. What steps would you take? Write down your description of the process.  

\paragraph{Extra challenge}  
Open a spreadsheet.  
\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item Create a new sheet.  
\item Rename the new sheet to 'My sheet'.  
\item Make a copy of 'My sheet'.  
\end{enumerate}  
Save your work.  

\paragraph{Think again}
You can make a copy of a sheet in a spreadsheet by following these steps:
\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item Open the spreadsheet.
\item Select the sheet you want to copy.
\item Use the "Duplicate" option or right-click and choose "Duplicate" to create a copy of the selected sheet.
\end{enumerate}  

\paragraph{Think again}
To change the name of a sheet in a spreadsheet, follow these steps:
\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item Open the spreadsheet.
\item Select the sheet you want to rename.
\item Use the "Rename" option or right-click and choose "Rename" to give a new name to the selected sheet.
\end{enumerate}  

