<<714>> Give me a combination of a design exercise and a short answer exercise for a 6th grade student learning computer science. <<Prompt>>
<<714>> You are going to create a poster about yourself. 
\begin{enumerate}
\item Make a plan for your poster. What text boxes and images will you use? 
\item Open a new file in a desktop publishing program. 
\item Add text boxes with the following headings: ‘Name', ‘Age', ‘Hobbies', ‘Favourite food', and ‘Favourite drink'. 
\item Add a text box for each heading and enter the information. 
\item Save your file and print your poster.
\end{enumerate} 

Think of other things you could add to your poster. What extra text boxes could you add? What extra images could you add? Think of how you could make your poster more interesting. Would you add more colours? Would you add more images? Would you use more fonts? Would you change the size of the text? Describe your ideas to a classmate. 

Now add extra text boxes and images to your poster. Save your file and print your new poster. 

Compare your new poster with your first one. What changes did you make? Which poster do you like best? Tell a classmate what you think. 

\begin{enumerate}
\item How could you improve your poster? 
\item What would you do if you had more time? 
