<<718>> Give me a combination of a temperature reading exercise and a comparison exercise for a 3rd grade student learning mathematics. <<Prompt>>
<<718>> The thermometer shows the temperature in a city.

\begin{enumerate}[label=\alph*.]
\item What is the temperature in the city?
\item Is it warmer in City A or City B?
\end{enumerate}

\begin{figure}[h!]
    \centering
\begin{tikzpicture}
    \begin{axis}[
        ybar,
        symbolic x coords={City A, City B},
        xtick=data,
        ymin=0, ymax=50,
        ylabel={Temperature (°C)},
        xlabel={City},
        bar width=0.5cm,
        nodes near coords,
        enlarge x limits=0.3,
        ytick={0,10,20,30,40,50}
    ]
        % Example data for City A and City B temperatures
        \addplot coordinates {(City A,35) (City B,20)};
    \end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
